WEBVTT

00:03.500 --> 00:06.410
Stop right there, purse-snatcher!

00:06.410 --> 00:08.330
You ain't catchin' me, girl!

00:08.830 --> 00:10.250
Stop!

00:10.250 --> 00:11.620
If you don't...

00:11.620 --> 00:13.830
I'll, I'll p-pomp you fulla holes!

00:13.830 --> 00:16.040
I'd like to see ya try!

00:30.500 --> 00:32.620
Looks like I caught you red-handed!

00:36.080 --> 00:40.830
I put my earphones in and curled up into a ball

00:41.290 --> 00:46.200
Armoring myself in that coccoon

00:52.040 --> 00:56.870
Even if my eyes only gaze upon a boring city

00:57.500 --> 01:02.330
My racing heart always longs for that sky

01:07.700 --> 01:16.040
Though yesterday's cuts still hurt

01:18.450 --> 01:23.200
I dreamt that today would be destroyed

01:23.200 --> 01:28.750
I struggle within, trying to burst forth as quickly as possible

01:28.750 --> 01:34.290
The walls around my heart are a planetarium of the sky

01:34.290 --> 01:39.500
I tremble as I open the nameless door

01:39.500 --> 01:45.120
I want to accept my wounds
and love the wind like a blue admiral butterfly

01:45.120 --> 01:50.330
I don't want to just look up at the sky

01:50.330 --> 01:56.160
I beg of myself to surpass my current self

01:56.450 --> 02:01.750
The coccoon has long since escaped from its cage

02:08.250 --> 02:09.500
Morning, Asuka.

02:10.200 --> 02:11.910
Yu?

02:12.450 --> 02:13.870
Mornin'...

02:15.450 --> 02:17.000
Are those...

02:17.330 --> 02:20.830
Yeah, the kids that this worlds'
Nana and Chloe are taking care of.

02:21.160 --> 02:23.080
They sure are energetic.

02:23.080 --> 02:25.750
I wonder if Kyo-chan and I were ever like that...

02:27.330 --> 02:30.790
But anyway, how freaky was that sexy Yu yesterday!

02:31.620 --> 02:36.500
Hey, Asuka, let's go rob a bank, c'mon!

02:42.080 --> 02:43.660
What the heck are you doing?!

02:43.660 --> 02:45.950
Flipping up your skirt, duh.

02:45.950 --> 02:48.370
I know that, but why?!

02:48.370 --> 02:53.200
Well, because I'm just sooo into you, Asuka!

02:53.700 --> 02:55.250
This Yu is really scary!

02:55.250 --> 02:57.870
What is wrong with you?
What world are you from, me?!

02:57.870 --> 03:05.830
Ugh, the fact that that's the thing I say in this
situation is so me, and sooo boring.

03:05.830 --> 03:08.700
I don't appreciate my own double calling me boring!

03:08.700 --> 03:12.950
Anyway, c'mon, Asuka! Let's rob a bank!

03:12.950 --> 03:15.830
I'll come by tomorrow with
something really awesome for it.

03:15.830 --> 03:18.410
You'll be super into it, Asuka, I guarantee you!

03:18.410 --> 03:19.410
Huh?

03:20.160 --> 03:22.790
I really want you to come with me.

03:22.790 --> 03:25.450
Yes, Mistress Yu!

03:26.870 --> 03:29.040
Asuka, why are you playing along with her?!

03:29.040 --> 03:30.750
Sorry, sorry, I got too worked up!

03:31.160 --> 03:33.410
That's my lovely Asuka for you!

03:34.250 --> 03:36.540
Bye, now! See you tomorrow!

03:39.660 --> 03:42.580
What was that weird Yu up to?

03:42.580 --> 03:46.040
Forget that, you're not really
going to rob a bank, are you?

03:46.040 --> 03:47.950
Oh no, I wouldn't!

03:51.410 --> 03:53.910
Sorry, there ain't much today.

03:53.910 --> 03:57.700
That's okay. I was thinkin'
I should go on a diet, anyway.

03:57.910 --> 04:01.200
We're pretty darn close to runnin' out of
the food we bought with our last haul.

04:01.450 --> 04:05.120
Until just a little while ago, we had a benefactor
who was helpin' us out pretty regularly.

04:04.040 --> 04:05.620
Aww, there's no more?

04:05.120 --> 04:06.830
But they up and disappeared.

04:05.620 --> 04:06.830
Wanna eat mine?

04:06.830 --> 04:08.080
Are you sure?

04:08.290 --> 04:11.410
These kids got no choice but to endure it all.

04:15.950 --> 04:19.040
Hi, Asuka! Good mornin'!

04:19.040 --> 04:21.870
We can carry anything we want with this right here!

04:22.950 --> 04:25.410
Hold on, Asuka! Think about what she's saying!

04:25.410 --> 04:28.580
I'll go! I'll help with the bank robbery!

04:33.160 --> 04:35.250
How many times do I have to tell you?!

04:35.250 --> 04:38.540
You've got the wrong girls! We told you that yesterday!

04:38.540 --> 04:44.830
How many times I gotta tell you
that I don't hear out the likes of bandits?

04:45.120 --> 04:46.660
C'mon, get to walkin'.

04:46.660 --> 04:49.830
Don't want the sun to set on us
before we get to the sheriff's.

04:50.200 --> 04:51.250
Wait!

04:51.450 --> 04:53.700
They're tellin' the truth.

04:53.700 --> 04:56.080
They're not your wanted criminals!

05:01.330 --> 05:03.790
A job well done, Silverstone.

05:01.510 --> 05:06.410
Sheriff's Office

05:03.790 --> 05:06.910
O-oh, I just got lucky.

05:07.120 --> 05:10.910
You were only that lucky 'cause you're
so darn passionate about upholdin' justice.

05:10.910 --> 05:12.370
Be proud of yourself.

05:12.790 --> 05:16.870
Maybe you're a better fit for the job
than I thought you were.

05:17.500 --> 05:21.120
The day we met, I thought,
there's no way in heck she'll make it.

05:21.540 --> 05:25.290
Huh? Then why'd you take me as your deputy?

05:25.290 --> 05:29.450
Well, 'cause you were the only one that applied.

05:30.450 --> 05:31.830
Is that why...

05:31.830 --> 05:35.330
But I had an inkling you might have it in you.

05:35.700 --> 05:39.290
'Specially when you came right up to me and said...

05:39.870 --> 05:40.950
Sheriff!

05:40.950 --> 05:44.830
I want to be a hero of justice for this town!

05:46.330 --> 05:52.500
Now that I think of it, I always wanted
to be a hero when I was a kid.

05:53.080 --> 05:56.910
But right around the end of elementary school,

05:56.910 --> 06:02.250
everyone started saying to me,
"Mia-chan, you must really like cute things, huh?"

06:02.250 --> 06:05.870
Well, given your appearance, I'm not surprised.

06:06.330 --> 06:10.040
On one hand, part of me thought they might be right,

06:10.040 --> 06:12.910
but another part of me thought they were totally wrong.

06:13.160 --> 06:17.370
Whenever I was talking about
cute stuff with my friends,

06:17.370 --> 06:21.330
that "not-cute" part of me somewhere
deep inside me felt really uncomfortable.

06:21.330 --> 06:22.870
I see...

06:22.870 --> 06:25.500
Don't know if an old man like myself
can fully understand your situation,

06:25.500 --> 06:30.040
but maybe that "not-cute" part'a you
was the one who brought you here.

06:30.370 --> 06:32.950
Yeah... That might be what happened.

06:33.250 --> 06:36.040
Has nobody ever tried to understand that part of you?

06:36.040 --> 06:38.250
The "not-cute" part, that is.

06:38.250 --> 06:39.080
Huh?

06:40.910 --> 06:44.660
I don't know, but maybe...

06:44.910 --> 06:47.290
Hey, new student! Yes, you!

06:47.290 --> 06:48.290
Yes?

06:48.440 --> 06:50.210
Crystal Radio Research Society
Now Accepting New Members!

06:49.200 --> 06:52.910
Wanna be the hero that saves
the Radio Research Society?

06:53.200 --> 06:54.540
Hero...

06:55.120 --> 06:56.540
Hero...

06:58.000 --> 07:01.040
Back then, Asuka-senpai...

07:01.540 --> 07:04.370
No, maybe I'm just overthinking it.

07:10.370 --> 07:13.790
Someone's pressed the emergency button
at El Akeyuki Bank!

07:13.790 --> 07:15.620
A bank robbery?!

07:17.080 --> 07:18.160
C'mon!

07:18.160 --> 07:19.250
Step on it!

07:21.750 --> 07:23.250
Adios!

07:23.250 --> 07:25.040
Don't you "Adios" me!

07:25.040 --> 07:27.450
They pressed the emergency button
because you weren't paying attention!

07:27.580 --> 07:29.700
Well, we got the cash, so it's all good!

07:29.700 --> 07:31.410
Now we just gotta get away!

07:31.790 --> 07:33.660
You stay here!

07:34.500 --> 07:35.500
What?!

07:35.750 --> 07:38.160
Making me stay here and do nothing...

07:46.540 --> 07:50.000
Go, go! Pedal to the metal, Sexy Yu!

07:50.000 --> 07:52.660
Take us beyond the confines of ecstasy!

07:52.660 --> 07:54.830
You're getting way too into this, Asuka.

07:55.700 --> 07:57.160
Oh, Asuka...

07:57.160 --> 07:58.080
Hyah!

08:00.620 --> 08:02.540
Giddy-up, li'l Chikuwa!

08:02.540 --> 08:05.500
Oh, that Asuka's not half bad, either...

08:05.500 --> 08:07.370
Wait, that's not important right now!

08:09.700 --> 08:13.160
I know you're the real criminals,
and I ain't lettin' you get away this time!

08:13.160 --> 08:14.870
Shoot, we're busted!

08:17.370 --> 08:24.040
I'm glad she let us go, but like, should we
really be working with that weird Asuka now?

08:24.040 --> 08:27.250
The girls she's after are us, you know!

08:27.250 --> 08:29.080
But they're real criminals.

08:29.080 --> 08:34.580
Plus, if they're forcing our Yu and Asuka
to help them, we've got to save them.

08:34.950 --> 08:37.500
You really think they were forced into it...?

08:37.870 --> 08:39.500
Well, whatever. Let's do this.

08:39.500 --> 08:40.370
Push!

08:43.750 --> 08:46.580
Aw, I thought I was gonna get
some more time to play around.

08:48.370 --> 08:50.080
Ciao, Asuka!

08:50.080 --> 08:51.410
Wait, what?!

08:51.410 --> 08:52.370
Whaaaa...?!

09:04.870 --> 09:06.750
Come out with your hands up!

09:06.750 --> 09:08.040
Ow, ow...

09:08.040 --> 09:09.200
Hey, it's me!

09:09.200 --> 09:11.660
What?! It's like I'm lookin' into a mirror!

09:11.660 --> 09:13.700
You're sayin' that now?

09:13.710 --> 09:15.140
Blockhead.

09:15.290 --> 09:16.790
Asuka! Yu!

09:17.120 --> 09:18.750
Hands up, all of you!

09:21.790 --> 09:24.750
What?! So many senpais!

09:28.290 --> 09:31.660
Umm, were you the ones who robbed the bank?

09:31.660 --> 09:34.250
N-no, Mia, you've got it all wrong!

09:34.250 --> 09:35.790
What's she got wrong?

09:35.790 --> 09:39.040
Ya'll're bona fide bank robbers!

09:42.410 --> 09:43.910
Sheriff Hakuma!

09:44.750 --> 09:46.250
The seven of you right there!

09:46.250 --> 09:49.500
You're all arrested for the crime of bank robbery!

09:49.500 --> 09:50.580
What?!

09:52.000 --> 09:53.040
What?!

09:57.510 --> 10:00.480
Courthouse

09:58.830 --> 10:00.450
I will now proceed with the sentencing!

10:00.750 --> 10:05.580
Nana Nanase and Chloé Morisu,
wanted criminals, and their two accomplices,

10:05.580 --> 10:08.450
50 years with hard labor.

10:08.870 --> 10:12.870
Furthermore, their accomplice Asuka Tsuchimiya
and her two accomplices,

10:12.870 --> 10:16.120
will be sentenced to 40 years with hard labor!

10:16.120 --> 10:17.950
I told you I wasn't workin' with them!

10:17.950 --> 10:19.870
Why am I gettin' rounded up with them?!

10:20.080 --> 10:21.830
I have already stated the reason.

10:22.370 --> 10:28.540
That was determined by Sheriff Hakuma's
eyewitness testimony and your actions at the scene!

10:30.870 --> 10:33.450
They really weren't workin' with us!

10:33.450 --> 10:35.450
We told you that already!

10:35.620 --> 10:41.120
Testimony from wanted criminals is not credible,
and thus, was not taken into consideration.

10:41.120 --> 10:42.580
What kind of trial is this?

10:42.580 --> 10:43.830
This is crazy!

10:44.080 --> 10:49.200
I'm amending your sentence to 60 years
with hard labor for contempt of court!

10:49.200 --> 10:50.160
What?!

10:50.160 --> 10:55.120
But seeing as the defendants are all young,
we may be able to reform them.

10:56.660 --> 11:00.450
In light of that, I'll do you a kindness.

11:00.450 --> 11:04.870
Both groups will duel.
The winner will be declared innocent!

11:04.870 --> 11:07.250
Hold it! Why've we gotta duel?!

11:07.250 --> 11:10.200
And wait, do us a kindness? That's pretty arrogant!

11:10.200 --> 11:13.500
I'm adding ten years hard labor
to both of your sentences!

11:13.500 --> 11:14.700
What is this, an all-you-can-sentence restaurant?!

11:14.700 --> 11:16.790
And another ten years!

11:17.040 --> 11:18.040
Court adjourned!

11:32.040 --> 11:33.540
Sheriff Hakuma!

11:34.870 --> 11:36.580
Why did you lie to her?

11:36.580 --> 11:37.580
What lie?

11:37.580 --> 11:39.410
You said they were all working together.

11:39.870 --> 11:43.540
I just told her what I saw, that's all.

11:43.870 --> 11:46.790
They were talking to one another all friendly-like.

11:46.790 --> 11:49.000
But I'm sure there was a reason for it!

11:49.000 --> 11:51.950
I thought I told you to toughen up, Silverstone!

11:51.950 --> 11:52.950
Huh?

11:52.950 --> 11:57.620
To make things right, we have to to avert our eyes
from contradictions and sacrifices.

11:57.620 --> 11:59.250
That's what true strength is.

11:59.250 --> 12:04.620
But Sheriff, you said we're the ones
who carry out justice.

12:04.620 --> 12:07.290
It is justice. My own kind of justice.

12:08.200 --> 12:13.200
That trial was a load of horse dung, but if we
go along with it, everything'll go right and well.

12:14.620 --> 12:17.750
I wouldn't expect a naive little thing
like you to understand.

12:17.750 --> 12:19.580
Run along now, get back to the station!

12:22.000 --> 12:23.160
Watch it!

12:23.410 --> 12:24.830
My apologies, sir.

12:24.830 --> 12:26.580
Sheriff, please, this really isn't-

12:28.290 --> 12:30.040
Lay low for a while.

12:30.040 --> 12:30.870
Huh?

12:33.330 --> 12:34.700
Asuka-san?

12:34.700 --> 12:37.620
So you really were the link this time.

12:37.950 --> 12:40.700
I freaked out when I saw who the defendants were.

12:40.700 --> 12:43.410
How'd you know the frequency for this world?

12:43.660 --> 12:46.160
We heard it on the radio.

12:46.160 --> 12:48.080
Forget that, my senpais are in danger!

12:48.080 --> 12:52.660
I know, but if you make a fuss now,
all my hard work will go to waste.

12:53.330 --> 12:56.040
I've got a chance to take out the Clutter in this world.

12:56.620 --> 12:59.830
Don't do anything, got it?

13:10.830 --> 13:14.700
As usual, I can't do anything to help anyone.

13:17.870 --> 13:19.750
Wait, is this...

13:22.750 --> 13:25.750
I'm so sorry, it just went flyin' off!

13:25.000 --> 13:27.370
For the Sheriff's Office

13:26.250 --> 13:27.370
It's okay.

13:27.370 --> 13:29.080
Thank you so much!

13:29.080 --> 13:32.450
Um, are you taking those to the sheriff's office?

13:32.450 --> 13:33.700
Yes?

13:33.700 --> 13:35.620
Let me take it instead!

13:37.080 --> 13:39.750
Oh... Well, thank you!

13:41.410 --> 13:43.540
The astral module.

13:51.330 --> 13:52.500
Get your beer here!

13:52.500 --> 13:54.950
Ice-cold beer! Come and get it!

13:55.660 --> 14:00.910
Look at the audience your perfect match-up
has brought in, Your Honor.

14:00.910 --> 14:03.040
Yes, thank goodness.

14:03.040 --> 14:07.830
I'm hearin' that the public viewing stations out in
the shopping district are full to the brim, too.

14:08.250 --> 14:12.330
You won't have any trouble takin' the crown
of number one fan favorite Judge.

14:14.750 --> 14:17.580
We will now begin the duel.

14:18.910 --> 14:21.540
When the music stops,

14:21.540 --> 14:26.040
draw your weapons and fire upon your opponents.

14:26.040 --> 14:29.830
You may fire as many times as it takes
to fell your opponent.

14:29.830 --> 14:33.410
However, if there is no clear winner to the duel,

14:33.410 --> 14:37.290
both parties will be executed.

14:37.660 --> 14:39.620
Good luck.

14:46.910 --> 14:49.660
I've gotta get this to Nana-senpai.

14:50.410 --> 14:52.540
Pardon me! Please let me through!

15:07.200 --> 15:09.120
There's no way I can shoot them.

15:10.040 --> 15:12.370
Draw your guns at once!

15:13.710 --> 15:14.710
I can't!

15:14.710 --> 15:16.830
I don't wanna!

15:19.370 --> 15:22.620
I thought they'd at least give us a little bit of a show.

15:23.580 --> 15:25.080
Kill-joys.

15:25.080 --> 15:27.870
I have no use for birds who won't sing for me.

15:27.870 --> 15:30.040
I suppose we'll have to execute them...

15:30.040 --> 15:33.200
That was a fine job you did, Sheriff Hakuma.

15:34.540 --> 15:37.200
Your request wasn't all that difficult
this time, Your Honor.

15:37.200 --> 15:42.700
It was right easy gettin' that bounty hunter and
those wanted criminals all arrested together.

15:43.450 --> 15:47.200
I'm sure a duel between a group of
cute young girls will really rake in the crowds.

15:47.200 --> 15:52.950
Even if they won't duel, and we have to kill them all,

15:52.950 --> 15:56.410
it should be quite a scene.

15:55.040 --> 15:56.410
Wh-what is this?!

15:56.410 --> 16:00.040
You'll be a shoo-in for most popular judge
this year, as always.

15:56.410 --> 15:58.830
Turn off those speakers right this instant!

16:03.290 --> 16:08.250
I took the liberty of recording
your conversation right before the trial.

16:08.500 --> 16:10.950
Here's where it gets juicy.

16:11.700 --> 16:15.040
The people of this town are so easy to manipulate.

16:15.040 --> 16:17.160
As long as you give them
something spectacular to look at,

16:17.160 --> 16:19.620
they'll all do so happily, wagging their loyal little tails.

16:20.500 --> 16:23.660
I mean, that's what I wanted, of course.

16:23.660 --> 16:26.580
Don't listen to it! This is nothing but a pack of lies!

16:26.580 --> 16:28.290
The hell's goin' on, Sheriff?

16:28.290 --> 16:30.040
You were in cahoots with the Judge the whole time?

16:30.700 --> 16:32.120
Sheriff...

16:32.790 --> 16:34.580
Please, everyone, calm down!

16:34.580 --> 16:36.660
Those voices are clearly fabricated!

16:36.910 --> 16:40.700
No... My power is fading!

16:40.950 --> 16:43.450
Come forth, my twilight self!

16:45.450 --> 16:47.250
Duplicate!

16:55.500 --> 16:57.700
Now you finally show yourself, Clutter!

16:58.250 --> 17:01.450
Your energy came from the support of the masses!

17:01.450 --> 17:03.500
Now that you're losing that support,

17:03.500 --> 17:06.160
you should be feeling extremely weak!

17:06.540 --> 17:08.500
You bitch!

17:13.750 --> 17:14.950
Why, you-

17:18.370 --> 17:20.040
You rotten kid!

17:25.330 --> 17:27.080
Two Clutters...?!

18:02.450 --> 18:03.580
Sheriff...

18:03.910 --> 18:06.830
You told me to be strong, but...

18:07.580 --> 18:10.580
I am strong, just not like you!

18:19.450 --> 18:20.370
Look!

18:20.830 --> 18:23.120
Come forth, my twilight self!

18:24.700 --> 18:26.450
Duplicate!

18:39.370 --> 18:41.080
I fight in the name of Justice!

18:42.120 --> 18:44.950
Mia Extreme!

18:46.290 --> 18:49.700
I'll keep the peace in this here world!

18:50.790 --> 18:52.790
Mia, you're an Equalizer!

18:53.040 --> 18:54.580
Justice Rush!

19:07.160 --> 19:08.330
Wow...

19:08.330 --> 19:09.500
She's strong...

19:09.790 --> 19:12.370
Mia really was a hero all along!

19:17.200 --> 19:19.200
Let's take them both out in one blow!

19:19.200 --> 19:20.250
Okay!

19:21.450 --> 19:23.290
Justice Rage Max!

19:23.290 --> 19:25.620
Double Hurricane!

19:29.200 --> 19:33.330
What no-good outlaws like you
deserve is a whole lotta lead.

19:44.410 --> 19:46.160
Just a little further...

19:46.500 --> 19:50.200
and this world would have been
sucked into the twilight.

19:57.750 --> 19:59.370
Silverstone...

20:00.290 --> 20:03.410
How did you get... so strong?

20:03.580 --> 20:05.830
I didn't suddenly get strong.

20:06.660 --> 20:08.370
It's just that your strength...

20:09.450 --> 20:11.000
...was never real.

20:26.870 --> 20:29.250
Hello, this is NanaChlo's House.

20:29.250 --> 20:32.580
A donation? Well, thank ya very much!

20:33.080 --> 20:34.830
Yes... Mm-hmm...

20:35.200 --> 20:39.200
Thanks to that trial, everyone knows
about our little orphanage.

20:39.540 --> 20:42.750
Lots of people are offerin' their help.

20:41.750 --> 20:42.750
Thank you.

20:42.750 --> 20:44.160
That's great.

20:44.410 --> 20:48.540
The bank even said they understood our situation
and would let us off the hook!

20:48.870 --> 20:51.410
This world is surprisingly laid-back.

20:51.790 --> 20:53.910
Let me make a donation, too.

20:55.330 --> 20:59.080
I can't offer much, but I wanna help.

20:59.410 --> 21:03.370
Donations are fine, but we could
really use a hand around here.

21:03.370 --> 21:07.370
She's right. I got the feeling
we're gonna be real good friends.

21:10.200 --> 21:12.370
I hate caterpillars!

21:11.080 --> 21:12.370
Wiggle, wiggle, wiggle!

21:12.370 --> 21:13.450
Wait up!

21:14.290 --> 21:15.540
Yeah...

21:16.370 --> 21:19.200
That there's the most decisive evidence
you could show me.

21:21.200 --> 21:24.500
It's about time for us to head home.

21:24.500 --> 21:26.120
Yeah, you're right.

21:26.790 --> 21:27.870
Bye-bye!

21:30.040 --> 21:31.080
Huh?

21:31.080 --> 21:32.330
What?

21:32.540 --> 21:34.370
Did you get a little taller?

21:34.370 --> 21:37.370
Yeah, you're right! You seem bigger somehow.

21:38.830 --> 21:41.250
It's 'cause I'm a hero of justice!

21:58.870 --> 22:05.950
I can't hear anything, I can't listen to anything

22:06.370 --> 22:13.950
Is it because my body has grown so much more adultlike now?

22:16.040 --> 22:23.790
The black radio on my bed, the first I ever bought

22:23.790 --> 22:31.620
Created so many melodies, so many generations

22:33.750 --> 22:40.290
Puberty changes a child into an adult

22:41.160 --> 22:48.450
I looked for a path, untainted as I was

22:49.000 --> 22:56.080
The dazzling crowd presses forward with no destination in mind

22:56.620 --> 23:03.910
Show them what true happiness is, broken-down radio

23:19.040 --> 23:23.950
I wanted to tell them not to go to another Fragment,
but I knew it wouldn't work.

23:23.950 --> 23:27.950
Especially with someone giving them the frequencies.

23:27.950 --> 23:29.580
Whoops, busted already?

23:29.910 --> 23:32.660
What Fragment are you from?

23:32.660 --> 23:34.330
Why are you interfering?

23:34.870 --> 23:38.870
Yes, why indeed...?
